{"id": "q0036", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1764770750, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "Crista's plants need to be watered every day. She has 20 plants. 4 of her plants need half of a cup of water. 8 plants need 1 cup of water. The rest need a quarter of a cup of water. How many cups of water does Crista need every day for her plants?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0036.wav", "input_sha256": "5f61fabab9dc509581bfbbe03c73104ffb653419ccf149b8d88942a1efae9cea", "input_samples": 315400, "input_s": 19.712, "n_real_chunks": 20, "score": 0.2141, "act": 0.9989, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so let's figure out how much water Krista needs for her plants. First, she has 4 plants that need half a cup each. So, 4 times 0.5 is 2 cups. Then, 8 plants need one cup each. That’s 8 times 1, which is 8 cups. Now, the rest of the plants are the ones that need a quarter cup. She has 20 total plants. We already accounted for 4 plus 8, which is 12. So, 2 0 minus 1 2 leaves us with 8 plants that need a quarter cup. Eigh t times 0.25 is 2 cups. Add ing it all together: 2 cups from the first group, 8 cups from the second, and 2 cups from the last group equal s 12 cup s. So, Kris ta needs 1 2 cups of water every day for her plants.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 19, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 45, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "