{"id": "q0074", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3813861270, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "A company produces chocolate in bars. In one day, it can produce 5000 bars. The company sells all the produced bars for $2 per bar. How much money will the company receive for selling produced chocolate bars during two weeks?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0074.wav", "input_sha256": "c8466ed485fce9e5d445ba4ff8d9bd6a718173c992aeac6535dd430d530c3b50", "input_samples": 293600, "input_s": 18.35, "n_real_chunks": 19, "score": 0.2029, "act": 0.998, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Let's break this down. First, we need to figure out how many bars are produced in two weeks. The company makes 5 00 0 bars each day. There are 7 days in a week, so in one week, they make 5 00 0 times 7, which is 3 5,00 0 bars. For two weeks, that’s 3 5,0 00 multiplied by 2, giving us 7 0,000 bars total. Each bar sells for $2, so the total revenue is 7 0,000 times 2, which equal s $140,00 0. So, the company will receive $1 40,000 from selling chocolate bars over two weeks.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 18, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 32, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0074_local_local.wav", "sha256": "43a1b0e516616ec9d838148172fd49cff013f2c7c732eabc9ddf8b19de63dbfd", "sr": 24000, "seco