{"id": "q0092", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2494721837, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "The caretaker of the docks needs to buy some new line. He wants 3 feet of line for every foot of dock. Right now, there is 200 feet of dock, and he has 6 feet of new line. How many feet of line does he need to buy in total?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0092.wav", "input_sha256": "04fd6f789b21f024f575aacbc061be0b1f1f9a108e29fd15a0135e0d03e281b6", "input_samples": 288800, "input_s": 18.05, "n_real_chunks": 19, "score": 0.2886, "act": 0.9995, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so he needs three feet of line for every foot of dock. Right now there's 200 feet of dock and he has six feet of new line. So first we need to figure out how much line he needs in total for the entire dock. He needs 3 feet of line for every foot of do ck, so that would be 2 00 times 3 which is 600 feet of line needed in total. But he already has 6 feet of line, so we subtract that from the total amount needed. 600 minus 6 equal s 59 4 feet. So he needs to buy 5 9 4 feet of line in total.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 14, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 32, "feed_lag_max_ms": 644, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 936, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0092_local_local.wav", "sha256": "9be8a15256abb0274d8f661194b9d463e40691135dc7d08b76fcf187aa50